<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a><a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a><main class="wrap inner-page academy-main" id="main-content"><section class="academy-page-hero"><div class="academy-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href='/resources'>Explore MBK</a></div><div class="academy-kicker">directory <span> / MBK GLOBAL</span></div><h1 class="page-title">Web Security Basics for Small Websites</h1><p class="page-intro">Foundational web security practices relevant to the web development and cybersecurity interests of Bakhtawar Khan (MBK).</p></section><p class="eyebrow">MBK NOTES · SEO / AEO / GEO</p><article class="identity-card"><p>Start with HTTPS, maintained dependencies, least-privilege access, strong authentication, safe form validation, secure headers, backups and a clear update process. Test only systems you own or are explicitly authorized to assess. Security is ongoing maintenance rather than a one-time badge. This article reflects general learning and practice guidance, not a claim of certification or a guarantee that any website is secure.</p><p><strong>About the author:</strong> Bakhtawar Khan (MBK) is the founder of MBK Global. His stated focus areas include web development, AI/API integration, cybersecurity learning, technical SEO and digital branding.</p><p><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Read the MBK Founder Profile ↗</a> · <a href="https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">MBK Global ↗</a> · <a href='/contact'>Discuss a project ↗</a></p></article><p class="page-intro">Published by Bakhtawar Khan · MBK Global. Content is educational and does not guarantee search rankings, security outcomes or AI citations.</p><section aria-label="Related MBK portfolio pages" class="mbk-related-links"><h2>Explore related MBK pages</h2><p>Continue exploring Bakhtawar Khan (MBK), MBK Global projects and practical digital technology resources.</p><ul><li><a href="/">Mr. Bakhtawar | Founder of MBK Global — Web Development, AI &amp; Digital Technology</a></li><li><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Mr. Bakhtawar | Founder of MBK Global</a></li><li><a href='/projects'>Projects by Bakhtawar Khan (MBK)</a></li><li><a href='/services'>Web Development, AI, APIs &amp; SEO Services | Bakhtawar Khan</a></li><li><a href='/resources'>Web Development, API, SEO &amp; Accessibility Resources | MBK</a></li><li><a href='/blog'>Articles &amp; Guides by Bakhtawar Khan (MBK)</a></li><li><a href='/official-links'>Official Links &amp; Projects</a></li><li><a href='/contact'>Contact Bakhtawar Khan (MBK)</a></li><li><a href='/cybersecurity'>Web Security Practices &amp; Review</a></li><li><a href='/web-security-basics-for-small-sites'>API Integration and Security Basics | Bakhtawar Khan (MBK)</a></li><li><a href='/web-security-basics-for-small-sites'>Privacy by Design for Small Projects | Bakhtawar Khan (MBK)</a></li></ul></section><section><h2 id="section-1">Implementation checklist</h2><ul><li>Keep privileged API keys on the server or in hosting environment variables, never in public browser code.</li><li>Validate and normalize user input at trust boundaries; encode output for its destination context.</li><li>Use HTTPS and configure security headers appropriate to the hosting provider.</li><li>Keep dependencies and integrations limited to what the site needs, and review updates before release.</li><li>Test contact forms without sending real messages; confirm validation and failure states locally.</li></ul></section><div data-portrait-track data-caption="A personal archive / Bakhtawar Khan"></div></main><script src="assets/js/script.js"></script><footer class="academy-footer"><div><a class="academy-brand personal-brand" href="/"><span>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global</small></span></a><p>Thoughtful technology. Useful knowledge. Work in progress.</p></div><nav aria-label="Footer"><a href='/resources'>Resources</a><a href='/official-links'>Official links</a><a href='/gallery'>Gallery</a><a href='/resume'>Resume</a><a href='/faq'>FAQ</a><a href='/privacy-policy'>Privacy</a></nav><div class="academy-colophon"><span>© 2026 Bakhtawar Khan · MBK Global</span><a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a></div></footer><script defer src="/assets/js/portfolio.js"></script><script defer src="/assets/js/visual-track.js"></script></body></html>